we're living on the cusp of the new  media age actually we're already deep  into it and when scholars can tear their  eyes away from the computer screen  they've looked back upon the history of  the book  now for jews no book has figured more  centrally  more profoundly in their history than  the bible  the jewish bible by the phrase the  jewish bible i mean the hebrew bible  that jews have actually held in their  hands and used not the text but the  physical object  whether it's been a scroll like the  monumental torah scroll or a book in the  course of history the material features  of these scrolls and books have changed  dramatically jews have developed laws  and rituals around them the objects  themselves come to possess their own  symbolic meaning this course requires no  previous background in jewish history or  judaism but it will take you on a tour  of jewish history from the ancient  period down until today  this course will teach you about many  things about the bible about judaism and  jewish history about jews christians and  muslims and how they've interacted but  more than anything else it will teach  you that a book is more than just words  on a page that has an object it has a  life of its own that is worth pondering  and understanding  [Music]
 

